  m_Name: 1960 spitting
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Spitting in Public Illegal 1960s
  info: 'Spitting in public spaces, such as sidewalks and parks, is banned to promote
    hygiene and prevent the spread of diseases. The anti-spitting law was introduced
    alongside other public health measures to combat illnesses like tuberculosis.
    Offenders are fined up to SGD 1,000 for first violations, with repeat offenses
    leading to even higher penalties. Public campaigns emphasize the health risks
    and social unacceptability of spitting in shared spaces.  '
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 88baf38a697df4a01a0ace0cf81a7f9e, type: 3}
